## Why This Is Asked
This question tests your ability to apply fundamental security controls to third-party components—a common real-world risk at many companies. It evaluates your understanding of vendor vetting, data minimization, privacy controls, and incident response readiness.

## Key Concepts
- Third-party risk management
- Data minimization and PII redaction
- User consent and privacy controls
- Observability and incident response readiness

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example: redact PII from analytics payload
function redact(payload) {
  const redacted = { ...payload };
  if (redacted.userEmail) redacted.userEmail = "[REDACTED]";
  if (redacted.userPhone) redacted.userPhone = "[REDACTED]";
  return redacted;
}

// Example: hash identifiers before transmission
function hashIdentifier(identifier) {
  return crypto.createHash('sha256').update(identifier).digest('hex');
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
This tests practical application of confidential computing to multi-tenant isolation in real-time ML workloads, beyond token-based controls.

## Key Concepts
- Confidential computing (TDX/Nitro/SEV)
- Per-tenant attested enclaves and key management
- Envelope encryption of in-flight data and outputs
- Attestation-based admission control at API gateway
- IR playbook with measurable success criteria

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-spec showing attestation flow
function attestedInference(req, enclave) {
  if (!enclave.attest(req.tenant)) throw new Error('Untrusted tenant');
  const input = enclave.declassify(req.input, req.tenant);
  const out = enclave.infer(input);
  return enclave.envelope(out, req.tenant);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you rotate per-tenant keys without service downtime?
- How would you detect and respond to a compromised enclave?

## Why This Is Asked
This question tests ability to design practical, compliant data access controls across serverless and containerized services, with ABAC, key management, RBAC, policy-as-code, and IR planning.

## Key Concepts
- ABAC attributes and enforcement points
- MongoDB Atlas RBAC & Client-Side Encryption
- AWS KMS key management and rotation
- Policy-as-code (OPA) integration and CI gates
- Incident response timing and evidence collection

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-authorization check example
function hasAccess(attrs, request) {
  const {service, tenant, data_class, operation, region} = attrs;
  const r = request;
  return r.service === service && r.tenant === tenant && r.data_class === data_class && r.operation === operation && r.region === region;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test ABAC policies in CI/CD and simulate breaches?
- How would you audit data access for forensics and regulatory reporting?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to translate data-security policy into concrete export controls.

## Key Concepts
- Data minimization and redaction
- RBAC and per-session scopes
- Token-based session gating
- Centralized exporting logs and retention
- IR playbooks and containment steps

## Code Example
```javascript
// Express route sketch: enforce role-based redaction on export
app.post('/exports/statements', authorize(['viewer','exporter']), (req,res)=>{
  const fields = req.user.role==='exporter' ? fullFields : ['date','amount','balance'];
  const csv = generateCSV(data, fields);
  res.setHeader('Content-Type','text/csv');
  res.send(csv);
});
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test the export redaction in CI?
- What metrics indicate success of the control?
